Create a class Order

Attributes:

customer_name (string)
items (list)
prices (list)
total_price (float)
is_paid (boolean)

def __init__(self, customer_name, items, prices, total_price, is_paid):
    self.customer_name = customer_name
    # continue

Methods:

def add_item(self, item_name, price)

This method should add the item_name to the items list and add the price to the prices list. Print the updated list of items.

def calculate_total(self)

This method should calculate the total price of all items using the prices list and update the self.total_price attribute. Print the total price.

def pay_order(self)

This method should change self.is_paid to True and print "Order has been paid".

def remove_item(self, item_name)

This method should remove an item from the items list (and its corresponding price from the prices list if it exists) and print the updated items list.

def get_order_summary(self)

Return all order information in a clear format including customer_name, items, total_price, and payment status.

Example format:
customer: Alex, items: ['Burger', 'Pizza'], total_price: 25.5, paid: False
